# Kaggle leaderboard integrity — these would let anyone "win" the public
# Kaggle competitions (food-level: tastebench-challenge-2026; molecular:
# molecular-taste-classification-2026) or de-anonymize the obfuscation
# (NECTAR ↔ Taste Like product mapping). Stay on disk locally; never ship.
kaggle_tastebench/generate_data/dataset/solution.csv
kaggle_tastebench/generate_data/dataset/product_code_map.csv
kaggle_tastebench/generate_data/dataset/competition_data.zip

# The withheld original-code -> public-code map, if you have been given it with
# the gated bundle. Matched by NAME at any depth, because it is a 4.5 KB JSON
# that is far easier to drop into a working tree and commit by accident than the
# rest of the gated data. Holding it is fine under the NDA; publishing it undoes
# the de-identification of every released artifact in one file.
product_code_map.json
kaggle_molecular_taste/dataset/solution.csv

# Derived caches (regeneratable from shared/scripts/prepare_caches/).
# compound_slice.parquet is deliberately NOT matched: it is 34 KB and ships.
shared/data/caches/*.pkl
shared/data/caches/*.csv
shared/data/caches/*.provenance.json
# Two things under caches/ DO ship and must stay tracked in a public repository.
# Both are release artifacts that happen to live beside the derived caches:
#   slices/  — the embedding caches cut to the 738 SMILES this benchmark reaches
#              (9.9 MB, replacing 1.9 GB; C29). The patterns above are per-file
#              globs, so the subdirectory was never matched — the exemption is
#              written out anyway, because the next person to add
#              `shared/data/caches/**` would silently drop the release payload.
#   sensory_descriptions.csv — the precomputed descriptions C21 promised to ship,
#              which the blanket *.csv rule above had been excluding.
!shared/data/caches/slices/
!shared/data/caches/slices/**
!shared/data/caches/sensory_descriptions.csv

# Heavy intermediates (regeneratable via food_similarity/prepare_data.py; the
# feature matrix is delivered by data/unpack_nectar_bundle.sh, see data/GATED.md)
food_similarity/data/product_features*.pkl

# Run-time outputs of reproduce.sh (regenerated every run).
food_similarity/results/cis_final_tables.csv
food_similarity/results/cis_final_tables.csv.sha256
food_similarity/results/repro_git_sha.txt

# Cached nested-LOOCV base features. Regenerated by the nested-CV runners in
# food_similarity/train/; npz files are deterministic given the input pkl.
food_similarity/results/cache/
